# GPS Toolset

Free GPS file tools at [gpstoolset.com](https://gpstoolset.com). Client-side parsing (no uploads). Clear · Private · Practical.

## Environments

- **Dev:** http://gpstoolset.lan/ → `/var/www/gpstoolset/public/`
- **Prod:** https://gpstoolset.com
- `base_url` env-aware. Never hardcode prod for local.

## Docs

- `docs/architecture.md` — **structure on disk** + request flow + how to add a tool
- `docs/plan.md` · `docs/cursor-prompts.md` · `docs/guides-brief.md` · `docs/design-direction.md` · `docs/seo-keywords.md`

## Stack

- PHP 8.4 · Apache · `.htaccess` / front controller · **no framework · no build step**
- Only `public/` is docroot; `config/`, `includes/`, `tools/`, `guides/`, `docs/` stay above it
- Vendored libs under `public/assets/vendor/` (Leaflet 1.9.4, Chart.js 4.4.7, GoPro GPMF bundles)

## Structure (P7 on disk)

```
config/tools.php          ← HTML route registry (viewers generated from formats.php)
config/formats.php        ← format registry (parser, exporter, detection, landing meta)
config/convert.php        ← converter SEO pairs
includes/router.php seo.php bootstrap.php
includes/layout/ pages/ partials/
tools/<slug>/{content,page}.php
  format landings: gpx|kml|kmz|fit-viewer + gopro → parse then viewer/
  gpx-editor/  convert/  gopro-gps-extract/  measure-distance/  coordinate-converter/
public/index.php          ← front controller + /sitemap.xml
public/assets/js/core|map|parsers|video|viewer|editor|converter|tools/
public/assets/css/{tokens,base,components,tool-landing,map-shell}.css
guides/ config/guides.php ← not created yet
```

- Shared **Track** model; edits in `core/edit.js` (used by `/gpx-editor`)
- **One generic viewer module** (`assets/js/viewer/`): format-agnostic; landings (incl. GoPro) parse then hand a track in. Refactor current gpx-viewer JS into it. GoPro adds GPMF + video only
- **One generic editor** (`assets/js/editor/`) and **one converter** (`assets/js/converter/`): same split — `/gpx-editor` and `/convert/...` are SEO landings that parse then hand off. Editor shares map/chart components with the viewer. **No duplicated map/chart code anywhere**
- **Menu:** Viewers (GPX, KML, KMZ, FIT, then a More section for GoPro) · Tools (Coordinate converter, Measure distance, Converter `/convert`)
- Converter SEO pairs under `/convert/<pair>`; old `/kml-to-gpx` etc. 301 → `/convert/...`
- Adding a **format** or convert pair = config + content only (no new JS). Full steps: `docs/architecture.md`
- Native ES modules; tiles only via `config/tiles.php` + `map/tiles.js`
- Sitemap from registry via `includes/seo.php`

## Privacy / chrome

- Parse in the browser only. Never upload user files.
- Privacy line OK on empty/pre-upload; **not** in header after load
- Privacy/About links **footer only**. No contact. No email / `mailto:`.

## Maps / OSM

- Central tile module only. Attribution **on the map only**.
- No © OSM in footer. No “Report a map issue”.

## Layout

- Map tools: full-screen map + slim top bar; dock under map; `gpstoolset.ui.v1`
- **No sample files.** Do not invent a demo track, a Sample button, or a “try a sample” file. The user opens their own file.
- `/gopro-gps-extract`: SEO landing → generic viewer for map · Video overlay (GPMF + video only)
- Ads: central partial; none on map tools at launch

## Design

- Tokens teal `#115e59` / `#2dd4a0` · orange `#c2410c` · route `#0369a1`
- Thin borders OK · **no heavy coloured one-sided accent borders**

## Content

- Never “Telemetry Extractor”. Never FlySight → “GNSS logger CSV exports”
- GoPro/DJI = compatibility wording; brand URL exception `/gopro-gps-extract` only
- May COPY from `/var/www/skylog`; **never edit** FlySync. No Highcharts.

## Git (hard rule — Paul)

- **Never** `git commit`, `git push`, `git amend`, or stage-and-commit
- Leave all changes **uncommitted** for Paul

## Workflow

- Verify at http://gpstoolset.lan/
- Leave changes uncommitted; Paul commits
- Do not edit `/etc/apache2` unless Paul asks
